                               https://mfem.org

This file describes the current Zig-based build for MFEM.

Requirements
============
- Zig 0.16.0
- A working C++17 toolchain for your platform

Quick start
===========
Default serial library build:
   zig build

Select the optimization mode explicitly:
   zig build -Doptimize=Debug
   zig build -Doptimize=ReleaseSafe

Useful build options
====================
Build a shared library:
   zig build -Dshared=true

Build in single precision:
   zig build -Dprecision=single

Enable MFEM exceptions:
   zig build -Dexceptions=true

Enable MFEM thread-safe internal code paths:
   zig build -Dthread-safe=true

Disable the internal MEMALLOC option:
   zig build -Dmemalloc=false

Enable MFEM SIMD code paths:
   zig build -Dsimd=true

Outputs
=======
- The generated library is installed under `zig-out/lib`
- Zig generates `config/_config.hpp` for the active build configuration

Current scope
=============
The current Zig migration covers the default serial MFEM library build.

The following areas are not yet wired into `build.zig`:
- MPI and hypre/METIS-based parallel builds
- Optional third-party libraries (PETSc, SUNDIALS, SuiteSparse, etc.)
- GPU backends and related dependencies
- Examples, miniapps, benchmarks, and unit tests

Documentation
=============
The Doxygen configuration lives in `doc/CodeDocumentation.conf.in`.
To generate the documentation directly with Doxygen:

   cd doc
   sed -e 's%@MFEM_SOURCE_DIR@%..%g' CodeDocumentation.conf.in > CodeDocumentation.conf
   doxygen CodeDocumentation.conf

The generated HTML entry point is `doc/CodeDocumentation/html/index.html`.
